  "label": "User projected onto the awe-expressing man as the embodiment of the stereotype",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the man_on_left (the man looking upward in awe) because the meme's text ('look dude a second hand store !!') directs the viewer's attention to his reaction, implying that the user is identifying with or imagining themselves as this character — someone who is thrilled by minimal resources like a second-hand store. This projection reinforces the harmful stereotype that Black people are lazy or content with poverty, and the user is implicitly positioned as the observer or participant in this caricatured scenario.",
